{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Read_2_ce27d6ea","content":"1\t# BUDGET — maintained by the harness (read-only for you)\n2\t\n3\t- Credits: 0.01 / 100.00 USD (0%)\n4\t- Time   : 0.0 h elapsed, 18.0 h remaining (0%)\n5\t- Phase  : normal\n6\t\n7\t## Harness notes\n8\t\n9\t- GPU: 0 min busy so far, peak memory 0.0 GiB"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Read_5_86ab4e27","content":"1\t\"\"\"Starter model written by the harness: log-normal martingale calibrated on the context.\n2\t\n3\tThis is a deliberately simple STARTING POINT — replace it with your own model.\n4\tContract: simulate(...) -> (start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths), each path has\n5\ttime_length//time_increment + 1 points starting at the context's last price.\n6\t\"\"\"\n7\t\n8\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n9\t\n10\timport numpy as np\n11\t\n12\t# Days of minute history simulate() receives as context_prices: a plain int from 3 to 30.\n13\tCONTEXT_DAYS = 7\n14\t\n15\t\n16\tdef simulate(\n17\t    asset: str,\n18\t    start_time,\n19\t    time_increment: int = 300,\n20\t    time_length: int = 86_400,\n21\t    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n22\t    context_prices=None,\n23\t):\n24\t    steps = time_length // time_increment + 1\n25\t    closes = context_prices[\"close\"].dropna()\n26\t    last = float(closes.iloc[-1])\n27\t    rets = np.diff(np.log(np.asarray(closes, dtype=float)))\n28\t    rets = rets[np.isfinite(rets)]\n29\t    per_step_sigma = float(np.std(rets)) * (time_increment / 60.0) ** 0.5 if rets.size > 10 else 1e-3\n30\t    rng = np.random.default_rng()\n31\t    shocks = rng.normal(0.0, per_step_sigma, size=(num_simulations, steps))\n32\t    shocks[:, 0] = 0.0\n33\t    paths = last * np.exp(np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1))\n34\t    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Read_8_2e226d6b","content":"1\t[project]\n2\tname = \"campaign-workspace\"\n3\tversion = \"0.1.0\"\n4\trequires-python = \">=3.12,<3.14\"\n5\tdependencies = [\"synth-lib\", \"numpy>=2.2\", \"pandas>=2.3\", \"torch>=2.0\"]\n6\t\n7\t[tool.uv.sources]\n8\t# rev is substituted by workspace.py with the commit the HOST was installed from, so the agent\n9\t# evaluates on the same library the verdict will score with.\n10\tsynth-lib = { git = \"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-lib\", rev = \"39bd62d28f9252ce744fe52d4ca68be73e51be94\" }"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Read_6_45e5d094","content":"1\t\"\"\"Self-evaluation via the official synth-lib backtester.\n2\t\n3\tUsage: uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-07-15\n4\tAnswers, with agent/modeling.py, the prompts the validator scored in the --days before --eval-end,\n5\tat the start times it actually used (read from the offline field bundle), then scores them with\n6\tbacktest() (validator CRPS + rank vs the real field, from the same bundle). A prompt is scored one\n7\thorizon after it starts, so generation begins one horizon before the scored days.\n8\t--cadence-minutes N answers an even grid over the same span instead; each scored prompt is then\n9\tanswered by the grid point at or before it.\n10\t\n11\t--crps-only scores CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid (--cadence-minutes,\n12\tby default every 60 minutes for 24h prompts and every 10 for 1h, on the round hour): no field, no\n13\trank, and any window of the snapshot, including before the bundle's span. Compare models on the same\n14\tgrid with it; it is not an absolute calibration level. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula.\n15\t\n16\tWorks on every asset. A minute without a trade is a flat candle with trade_count 0. Prices load\n17\tthrough the same lenient path the scored evaluation uses, so a NaN close (no price at all) reaches\n18\tsimulate() rather than stopping the run — your model must tolerate them (drop, never interpolate).\n19\tThe context spans the CONTEXT_DAYS your modeling.py sets (7 without it), and the days before an\n20\tasset's first trade, or before the snapshot's first day, are NaN.\n21\t\n22\tWhen the snapshot carries an event calendar ($SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR), the summary is followed by\n23\tyour gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type and\n24\tover those that hold none: where an event costs you, that gap is wider.\n25\t\n26\t--num-simulations defaults to 1000, matching the validator's real serving size\n27\t(PromptConfig.num_simulations). Lowering it (e.g. for a quick local iteration loop) speeds up\n28\tgeneration at the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS: empirical CRPS is biased upward for\n29\tfewer sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000.\n30\t\n31\tThe context a prompt gets ends BEFORE its start_time, and that is not an off-by-one. The store\n32\tlabels a minute bar by its OPEN time, so the bar labelled t closes at t+60s — and that close is\n33\tthe first point the prompt is scored against. A prompt is also issued before the start_time it is\n34\tscored from (ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS). Ending the context at t would hand the model the answer to\n35\tits own first step, and a model tuned that way is optimising a problem it will not be scored on.\n36\t\"\"\"\n37\t\n38\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n39\t\n40\timport argparse\n41\timport json\n42\timport os\n43\timport shutil\n44\timport sys\n45\timport tempfile\n46\tfrom datetime import datetime, timedelta, timezone\n47\tfrom pathlib import Path\n48\t\n49\timport numpy as np\n50\timport pandas as pd\n51\t\n52\tfrom synth_lib.backtester.config import PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES\n53\tfrom synth_lib.backtester.loading import get_miner_scores\n54\tfrom synth_lib.backtester.orchestration import backtest, score_crps\n55\tfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import (\n56\t    context_days_of,\n57\t    context_slice,\n58\t    load_minute_prices,\n59\t    nan_head_minutes,\n60\t)\n61\tfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\n62\tfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_ENV, concerns\n63\t\n64\t# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\n65\t# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\n66\t# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\n67\tAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n68\tWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\n69\tsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\n70\t\n71\timport modeling  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)\n72\t\n73\t# Your modeling.py's CONTEXT_DAYS, read as the verdict and the live miner read it.\n74\tCONTEXT_DAYS = context_days_of(modeling)\n75\t# Each run writes its predictions to its own directory under this one.\n76\tPREDICTIONS_ROOT = WORKSPACE / \"miner_outputs\" / \"campaign\"\n77\t# Must match synth_lib.backtester.config._OFFLINE_ENV_VAR.\n78\tOFFLINE_ROOT_ENV = \"SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT\"\n79\t# backtest()'s default miner_id: the rows of prompt_df that are yours.\n80\tCANDIDATE_ID = 999\n81\t# The --crps-only grid, by time_length. Must match synth_lib.benchmark.verdict.run_verdict.CADENCE_MINUTES.\n82\tCRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES = {86_400: 60, 3_600: 10}\n83\t\n84\t\n85\tdef ensure_workspace_cwd() -> None:\n86\t    \"\"\"Force the cwd to the workspace root.\n87\t\n88\t    NECESSARY: synth-lib's `backtest()` resolves the realized-price store via\n89\t    `MinutePriceStore(asset)` WITHOUT an explicit root (see `_price_store`), so it resolves\n90\t    relative to the cwd. Launched from agent/, it would look for `agent/market_data/`, find\n91\t    nothing, and attempt an `ingest_range` (download + write) against a snapshot mounted\n92\t    READ-ONLY — a cryptic error. The snapshot is mounted at the workspace root: we move there.\"\"\"\n93\t    os.chdir(WORKSPACE)\n94\t\n95\t\n96\tdef require_offline_bundle() -> None:\n97\t    \"\"\"Fails unless backtest() reads the field from the offline bundle.\n98\t\n99\t    backtest() reads scores and rewards a day past --eval-end; from the live API that is data from\n100\t    after your cutoff.\"\"\"\n101\t    if not os.environ.get(OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV):\n102\t        raise SystemExit(\n103\t            f\"{OFFLINE_ROOT_ENV} is not set, so backtest() would read the field from the live API, past \"\n104\t            f\"--eval-end. The harness points it at the bundle in your snapshot; restore it.\"\n105\t        )\n106\t\n107\t\n108\tdef store_root(asset: str) -> Path:\n109\t    \"\"\"Where this asset's partitions live inside the snapshot.\n110\t\n111\t    Resolved by synth-lib rather than hardcoded: the canonical directory is `market_data/prices/`,\n112\t    with a fallback to the legacy `market_data/pyth/` when that is what the snapshot contains. Do\n113\t    Anchored on WORKSPACE, not the cwd — synth-lib's default_store_root() resolves relative to the\n114\t    cwd, which would break the invariant this file relies on everywhere else.\"\"\"\n115\t    return WORKSPACE / \"market_data\" / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n116\t\n117\t\n118\tdef check_snapshot_coverage(asset: str, start: datetime, end: datetime, first_prompt: datetime) -> None:\n119\t    \"\"\"Fails EARLY and clearly if the requested window falls outside the frozen snapshot.\n120\t\n121\t    The context's days before the asset's first partition are not missing: the context holds them\n122\t    as NaN. The days from the first prompt on are never exempt.\n123\t    Without this guard, synth-lib would try to ingest the missing days (network + write) and\n124\t    the error would surface in an unreadable form.\"\"\"\n125\t    root = store_root(asset)\n126\t    first = min((p.name for p in root.glob(\"date=*.parquet\")), default=\"\")\n127\t    holes_from = min(first, f\"date={first_prompt.date().isoformat()}.parquet\")\n128\t    missing = []\n129\t    cursor = start.date()\n130\t    while cursor <= end.date():\n131\t        name = f\"date={cursor.isoformat()}.parquet\"\n132\t        if name >= holes_from and not (root / name).exists():\n133\t            missing.append(cursor.isoformat())\n134\t        cursor += timedelta(days=1)\n135\t    if missing:\n136\t        raise SystemExit(\n137\t            f\"window outside snapshot for {asset}: missing partitions {missing[:5]}\"\n138\t            f\"{' …' if len(missing) > 5 else ''}\\n\"\n139\t            f\"The snapshot is frozen (read-only): it ends at the campaign's data_cutoff, and DATA.md gives \"\n140\t            f\"each asset's first and last day. Choose --eval-end / --days so that the window and its \"\n141\t            f\"CONTEXT_DAYS stay on days {root} holds.\"\n142\t        )\n143\t\n144\t\n145\tdef prompt_times(\n146\t    asset: str,\n147\t    end: datetime,\n148\t    days: int,\n149\t    time_length: int,\n150\t    time_increment: int,\n151\t    cadence_minutes: int | None = None,\n152\t) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:\n153\t    \"\"\"Start times of the prompts scored in the `days` before `end`: the validator's own, from the\n154\t    offline bundle, or every `cadence_minutes` over the same span.\"\"\"\n155\t    first = end - timedelta(days=days)\n156\t    if cadence_minutes is not None:\n157\t        horizon = timedelta(seconds=time_length)\n158\t        return list(pd.date_range(first - horizon, end - horizon, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", inclusive=\"left\"))\n159\t    scores = get_miner_scores(first, end, asset, time_length, time_increment)\n160\t    if scores.empty:\n161\t        raise SystemExit(\n162\t            f\"the offline bundle has no scored {asset} prompt for --time-length {time_length} in \"\n163\t            f\"{first.date()} → {end.date()} (DATA.md gives its span); --crps-only scores CRPS alone \"\n164\t            f\"on any window of the snapshot.\"\n165\t        )\n166\t    return sorted(pd.to_datetime(scores[\"start_time\"], utc=True).unique())\n167\t\n168\t\n169\tdef generate(\n170\t    asset: str,\n171\t    times: list[pd.Timestamp],\n172\t    out_dir: Path,\n173\t    time_increment: int = 300,\n174\t    time_length: int = 86_400,\n175\t    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n176\t) -> int:\n177\t    # The same loader the scored evaluation uses. NOT MinutePriceStore.load_range, which raises\n178\t    # on a single NaN close. NaN reaches simulate() untouched, which is the contract — never\n179\t    # interpolate it away.\n180\t    prices = load_minute_prices(WORKSPACE / \"market_data\", asset, times[0] - pd.Timedelta(days=CONTEXT_DAYS), times[-1])\n181\t    out_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n182\t    head = 0\n183\t    for t in times:\n184\t        # Never `prices.loc[:t]` — see the module docstring. Same cut the scored evaluation uses.\n185\t        context = context_slice(prices, t, time_length, CONTEXT_DAYS)\n186\t        head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))\n187\t        out = modeling.simulate(\n188\t            asset=asset,\n189\t            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n190\t            time_increment=time_increment,\n191\t            time_length=time_length,\n192\t            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n193\t            context_prices=context,\n194\t        )\n195\t        paths = [list(map(float, p)) for p in out[2:]]\n196\t        record = {\n197\t            \"start_timestamp\": t.isoformat(),\n198\t            \"asset\": asset,\n199\t            \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n200\t            \"time_length\": time_length,\n201\t            \"num_simulations\": len(paths),\n202\t            \"num_steps\": len(paths[0]),\n203\t            \"paths\": paths,\n204\t        }\n205\t        name = t.strftime(\"%Y-%m-%d_%H:%M:%SZ\") + f\"_{asset}_{time_length}.json\"\n206\t        (out_dir / name).write_text(json.dumps(record))\n207\t    if head:\n208\t        print(\n209\t            f\"warning: {asset} contexts start with up to {head / 1440:.1f} days of NaN, before its first price \"\n210\t            f\"in the snapshot\"\n211\t        )\n212\t    return len(times)\n213\t\n214\t\n215\tdef print_event_split(prompts: pd.DataFrame, asset: str, time_length: int) -> None:\n216\t    \"\"\"Your gap to each prompt's best miner, over the prompts whose horizon holds an event of each type\n217\t    and over the prompts that hold none.\"\"\"\n218\t    path = Path(os.environ[CALENDAR_ENV])\n219\t    if not path.exists():\n220\t        return\n221\t    view = pd.read_parquet(path)\n222\t    view = view[concerns(view, asset)]\n223\t    scored = prompts[prompts[\"crps\"] > 0]  # -1 marks a prompt the backtester could not score\n224\t    best = scored.groupby([\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])[\"crps\"].min().rename(\"best\")\n225\t    ours = scored[scored[\"miner_id\"] == CANDIDATE_ID].join(best, on=[\"asset\", \"scored_time\"])\n226\t    if ours.empty:\n227\t        return\n228\t    gap = ours[\"crps\"].to_numpy() / ours[\"best\"].to_numpy() - 1\n229\t    starts = pd.to_datetime(ours[\"start_time\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy()\n230\t    ends = starts + np.timedelta64(time_length, \"s\")\n231\t    spans_any = np.zeros(len(ours), dtype=bool)\n232\t    lines = []\n233\t    for event, rows in view.groupby(\"event\"):\n234\t        times = np.sort(pd.to_datetime(rows[\"time_utc\"], utc=True).dt.tz_localize(None).to_numpy())\n235\t        at = np.searchsorted(times, starts)\n236\t        spans = (at < len(times)) & (times[np.minimum(at, len(times) - 1)] < ends)\n237\t        spans_any |= spans\n238\t        if spans.any():\n239\t            lines.append(f\"  {event:<17} {spans.sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[spans].mean():+.2%}\")\n240\t    if not spans_any.all():\n241\t        lines.insert(0, f\"  {'no event':<17} {(~spans_any).sum():5d} prompts  gap {gap[~spans_any].mean():+.2%}\")\n242\t    print(\"event split (mean gap to each prompt's best miner):\")\n243\t    print(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n244\t\n245\t\n246\tdef main() -> None:\n247\t    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n248\t    ap.add_argument(\"--asset\", default=\"BTC\")\n249\t    ap.add_argument(\"--days\", type=int, default=3)\n250\t    ap.add_argument(\"--eval-end\", required=True, help=\"YYYY-MM-DD, at most the snapshot's last day\")\n251\t    ap.add_argument(\"--time-increment\", type=int, default=300, help=\"seconds between points (60 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n252\t    ap.add_argument(\"--time-length\", type=int, default=86_400, help=\"horizon in seconds (3600 for CRYPTO_1H)\")\n253\t    ap.add_argument(\n254\t        \"--num-simulations\",\n255\t        type=int,\n256\t        default=1000,\n257\t        help=\"Paths per prompt. The validator uses 1000; lowering this speeds up iteration at \"\n258\t        \"the cost of a slightly pessimistic CRPS (empirical CRPS is biased upward for fewer \"\n259\t        \"sampled paths, and the real field's CRPS was computed at 1000).\",\n260\t    )\n261\t    ap.add_argument(\n262\t        \"--cadence-minutes\",\n263\t        type=int,\n264\t        default=None,\n265\t        help=\"answer an even grid every N minutes instead of the validator's own start times (with \"\n266\t        \"--crps-only, 60 for 24h prompts and 10 for 1h by default). A cadence that divides an hour \"\n267\t        \"puts every prompt on the round hour\",\n268\t    )\n269\t    ap.add_argument(\n270\t        \"--latest-formula\",\n271\t        action=\"store_true\",\n272\t        help=\"score every crypto-1h prompt with the volatility term, as prompts are scored now, \"\n273\t        \"including those scored before it went live. Field ranks before that day then compare \"\n274\t        \"two formulas; CRPS does not\",\n275\t    )\n276\t    ap.add_argument(\n277\t        \"--crps-only\",\n278\t        action=\"store_true\",\n279\t        help=\"CRPS alone, against the snapshot's own prices, on an even grid: no field and no rank, \"\n280\t        \"on any window of the snapshot. crypto-1h is scored with the latest formula\",\n281\t    )\n282\t    ap.add_argument(\"--keep-predictions\", action=\"store_true\", help=\"keep this run's prediction files\")\n283\t    args = ap.parse_args()\n284\t    if not args.crps_only:\n285\t        require_offline_bundle()\n286\t    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n287\t    end = datetime.fromisoformat(args.eval_end).replace(tzinfo=timezone.utc)\n288\t    cadence = args.cadence_minutes\n289\t    if args.crps_only:\n290\t        cadence = cadence or CRPS_ONLY_CADENCE_MINUTES[args.time_length]\n291\t    times = prompt_times(args.asset, end, args.days, args.time_length, args.time_increment, cadence_minutes=cadence)\n292\t    # the context reaches back CONTEXT_DAYS before the first prompt: coverage must extend that far\n293\t    check_snapshot_coverage(args.asset, times[0] - timedelta(days=CONTEXT_DAYS), end, times[0])\n294\t    PREDICTIONS_ROOT.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n295\t    out_dir = Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"run-\", dir=PREDICTIONS_ROOT))\n296\t    try:\n297\t        n = generate(\n298\t            args.asset,\n299\t            times,\n300\t            out_dir,\n301\t            time_increment=args.time_increment,\n302\t            time_length=args.time_length,\n303\t            num_simulations=args.num_simulations,\n304\t        )\n305\t        print(f\"predictions generated: {n}\")\n306\t        if args.crps_only:\n307\t            result = score_crps(\n308\t                miner_name=\"campaign\",\n309\t                asset=args.asset,\n310\t                time_length=args.time_length,\n311\t                time_increment=args.time_increment,\n312\t                predictions_dir=out_dir,\n313\t            )\n314\t            print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {CONTEXT_DAYS}):\", result.summary)\n315\t            return\n316\t        result = backtest(\n317\t            miner_name=\"campaign\",\n318\t            asset=args.asset,\n319\t            time_length=args.time_length,\n320\t            time_increment=args.time_increment,\n321\t            n_backtest_days=args.days,\n322\t            predictions_dir=out_dir,\n323\t            eval_end=end,\n324\t            latest_formula=args.latest_formula,\n325\t            match_tolerance_minutes=args.cadence_minutes or PREDICTION_MATCH_TOLERANCE_MINUTES,\n326\t        )\n327\t        print(f\"summary (CONTEXT_DAYS {CONTEXT_DAYS}):\", result.summary)\n328\t        if os.environ.get(CALENDAR_ENV):\n329\t            print_event_split(result.prompt_df, args.asset, args.time_length)\n330\t    finally:\n331\t        if args.keep_predictions:\n332\t            print(f\"predictions kept in {out_dir}\")\n333\t        else:\n334\t            shutil.rmtree(out_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n335\t\n336\t\n337\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n338\t    main()"}
