{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Read_28_b83a739c","content":"1\t\"\"\"Generate predictions from a modeling.py over a prompt grid — the reusable evaluation core.\n2\t\n3\tDELIBERATELY SELF-CONTAINED: imports nothing from synth_lib, only numpy/pandas/stdlib. It is\n4\tcopied into a champion's clone and executed inside a --network none sandbox whose venv holds only\n5\tthe champion's own pins, so a synth_lib import here would break every verdict.\n6\tThat is what lets it serve three duties with one implementation:\n7\t  - the verdict runner copies this single file into a cloned champion workspace and runs it\n8\t    inside the --network none sandbox (synth_lib/benchmark/verdict/run_verdict.py);\n9\t  - the CI contract gate runs it on the host against any miner exposing simulate();\n10\t  - an operator can run it standalone against any modeling.py.\n11\t\n12\tNo-lookahead guarantee: for each prompt at time t the model receives only what a miner answering\n13\tthat prompt could have held. The validator issues a prompt BEFORE the start_time it scores from\n14\t(ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS), and the store labels a minute bar by its OPEN time, so the bar labelled t\n15\tcloses at t + 60s and its close is the first point the prompt is scored against. Ending the context\n16\tat t would therefore hand the model that exact value. The context ends one bar before the issuance\n17\tinstead. The model's sole market input is that DataFrame; simulate() takes no data root.\n18\t\n19\tPredictions land one file per day, under\n20\t`<out>/<asset>/<time_length>_<time_increment>/date=<YYYY-MM-DD>.npy` — float32, shaped\n21\t(prompts, simulations, steps) — beside a `.json` naming the prompt start_times it holds, the\n22\tchampion's CONTEXT_DAYS and `context_head_nan_minutes`, the most minutes one of the day's contexts\n23\truns before its first real close. A day whose file already covers every requested start_time is\n24\tskipped, so pointing --out-dir at a directory that survives the run makes a re-score reuse the paths\n25\tinstead of regenerating them, with the contexts they were generated from.\n26\t\n27\tUsage:\n28\t  python generate_predictions.py --modeling agent/modeling.py --asset BTC \\\\\n29\t      --window-start 2026-07-30 --window-end 2026-08-03 \\\\\n30\t      --data-root market_data --out-dir predictions \\\\\n31\t      --time-increment 300 --time-length 86400 --cadence-minutes 60\n32\t\"\"\"\n33\t\n34\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n35\t\n36\timport argparse\n37\timport importlib.util\n38\timport json\n39\timport sys\n40\tfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n41\tfrom pathlib import Path\n42\tfrom types import ModuleType\n43\tfrom typing import Callable\n44\t\n45\timport numpy as np\n46\timport pandas as pd\n47\t\n48\t# The champion's context length: `CONTEXT_DAYS` in its modeling.py, a plain int within these bounds,\n49\t# and this default when the module does not set it.\n50\tDEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS = 7\n51\tCONTEXT_DAYS_BOUNDS = (3, 30)\n52\t# Duplicated from synth_lib.preparation.config rather than imported: this file runs inside a\n53\t# champion's own venv, which does not have synth_lib.\n54\tOHLCV_COLUMNS = [\"open\", \"high\", \"low\", \"close\", \"volume\", \"trade_count\"]\n55\t# The validator's real serving size (PromptConfig.num_simulations). Empirical CRPS is biased\n56\t# upward for small N, so scoring at fewer paths than the field unfairly penalizes the candidate.\n57\tDEFAULT_NUM_SIMULATIONS = 1000\n58\tSTORE_SUBDIR = \"prices\"\n59\t# How far before a prompt's start_time the validator issues it, per format — measured from\n60\t# `validator_requests.request_time - start_time`. A miner answers within seconds of issuance, so\n61\t# nothing that closes after this instant can be in its hands.\n62\tISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS = {3_600: 60, 86_400: 120}\n63\t# The store's bar width. A bar labelled b covers [b, b+BAR_SECONDS), so its close is known only at\n64\t# b + BAR_SECONDS; the newest bar a miner holds at time c is the one labelled c - BAR_SECONDS.\n65\tBAR_SECONDS = 60\n66\t\n67\t\n68\tdef context_end(start: pd.Timestamp, time_length: int, issuance_lead: int | None = None) -> pd.Timestamp:\n69\t    \"\"\"Label of the last bar a miner answering the prompt at `start` could have held.\"\"\"\n70\t    lead = ISSUANCE_LEAD_SECONDS.get(time_length, 0) if issuance_lead is None else issuance_lead\n71\t    return start - pd.Timedelta(seconds=lead + BAR_SECONDS)\n72\t\n73\t\n74\tdef context_slice(\n75\t    frame: pd.DataFrame, start: pd.Timestamp, time_length: int, context_days: int, issuance_lead: int | None = None\n76\t) -> pd.DataFrame:\n77\t    \"\"\"The context of the prompt at `start`: the bars from `context_days` before it to `context_end`.\"\"\"\n78\t    return frame.loc[start - pd.Timedelta(days=context_days) : context_end(start, time_length, issuance_lead)]\n79\t\n80\t\n81\tdef nan_head_minutes(context: pd.DataFrame) -> int:\n82\t    \"\"\"How many minutes the context runs before its first real close.\"\"\"\n83\t    real = context[\"close\"].notna().to_numpy()\n84\t    return int(real.argmax()) if real.any() else len(real)\n85\t\n86\t\n87\tdef context_days_of(module: ModuleType) -> int:\n88\t    \"\"\"The champion's `CONTEXT_DAYS`, or the default when its module does not set it.\"\"\"\n89\t    value = getattr(module, \"CONTEXT_DAYS\", DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS)\n90\t    low, high = CONTEXT_DAYS_BOUNDS\n91\t    if type(value) is not int or not low <= value <= high:\n92\t        raise ValueError(f\"CONTEXT_DAYS must be a plain int from {low} to {high} in modeling.py, got {value!r}\")\n93\t    return value\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t# What simulate() receives as context_prices: the minute OHLCV frame, or the Series of closes (NaN\n97\t# kept) of the contract before OHLCV, for a champion written against that one.\n98\tCONTEXT_MODES = (\"ohlcv\", \"close\")\n99\t\n100\t\n101\t# float32 is what the validator stores miner predictions as, so the field's CRPS was computed at\n102\t# this precision too. It also quarters the cache: a day of crypto-1h is 35 MB instead of 170.\n103\tPATH_DTYPE = \"float32\"\n104\t\n105\t\n106\tdef day_files(out_dir: Path, asset: str, time_length: int, time_increment: int, day: str) -> tuple[Path, Path]:\n107\t    \"\"\"The (paths, index) pair for one day of one prompt format.\"\"\"\n108\t    root = out_dir / asset / f\"{time_length}_{time_increment}\"\n109\t    return root / f\"date={day}.npy\", root / f\"date={day}.json\"\n110\t\n111\t\n112\tdef covered_start_times(index_path: Path, paths_path: Path) -> set[str]:\n113\t    \"\"\"Prompt start_times the day file already holds, or nothing when it has none.\n114\t\n115\t    Both halves must be present. build_prediction_index skips an index whose .npy is missing, so\n116\t    treating that state as covered here would skip generation for a day nothing can then score.\n117\t    \"\"\"\n118\t    if not (index_path.exists() and paths_path.exists()):\n119\t        return set()\n120\t    try:\n121\t        return set(json.loads(index_path.read_text())[\"start_times\"])\n122\t    except (ValueError, KeyError):\n123\t        return set()  # truncated by an interrupted write; regenerate the day\n124\t\n125\t\n126\tdef load_module(modeling_path: Path) -> ModuleType:\n127\t    # A champion imports the modules beside it by name, as when its folder is the script's own.\n128\t    folder = str(modeling_path.resolve().parent)\n129\t    if folder not in sys.path:\n130\t        sys.path.insert(0, folder)\n131\t    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(f\"candidate_{modeling_path.parent.name}\", modeling_path)\n132\t    assert spec is not None and spec.loader is not None  # always true for a .py file path\n133\t    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n134\t    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n135\t    return module\n136\t\n137\t\n138\tdef load_simulate(modeling_path: Path) -> Callable:\n139\t    return load_module(modeling_path).simulate\n140\t\n141\t\n142\tdef store_root(data_root: Path, asset: str) -> Path:\n143\t    root = data_root / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n144\t    if not root.exists():\n145\t        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"no minute store for {asset}: {root} does not exist\")\n146\t    return root\n147\t\n148\t\n149\tdef load_minute_prices(data_root: Path, asset: str, start: pd.Timestamp, end: pd.Timestamp) -> pd.DataFrame:\n150\t    \"\"\"Minute OHLCV over [start, end] from daily partitions.\n151\t\n152\t    The days before the asset's first partition, before the market's first trade or the store's first\n153\t    day, are NaN on every minute, as in a live context. A missing partition after it raises: a silent\n154\t    hole here would shrink every context that spans it without anyone noticing.\"\"\"\n155\t    root = store_root(data_root, asset)\n156\t    stored = (date.fromisoformat(p.stem.removeprefix(\"date=\")) for p in root.glob(\"date=*.parquet\"))\n157\t    first_day = min(stored, default=start.date())\n158\t    frames = []\n159\t    day = max(start.date(), first_day)\n160\t    while day <= end.date():\n161\t        path = root / f\"date={day.isoformat()}.parquet\"\n162\t        if not path.exists():\n163\t            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"missing partition {path}\")\n164\t        try:\n165\t            frames.append(pd.read_parquet(path, columns=[\"timestamp\", *OHLCV_COLUMNS]))\n166\t        except ValueError as exc:  # pyarrow's ArrowInvalid, on a column the file lacks\n167\t            raise ValueError(\n168\t                f\"{path} predates the OHLCV columns. Re-ingest with --force-refresh: ingest_day \"\n169\t                f\"skips settled partitions that already exist.\"\n170\t            ) from exc\n171\t        day += timedelta(days=1)\n172\t    if not frames:\n173\t        raise FileNotFoundError(\n174\t            f\"no partition for {asset} from {start.date()} to {end.date()}: its first is {first_day}\"\n175\t        )\n176\t    frame = pd.concat(frames, ignore_index=True)\n177\t    frame[\"timestamp\"] = pd.to_datetime(frame[\"timestamp\"], utc=True)\n178\t    frame = frame.set_index(\"timestamp\").sort_index()\n179\t    if start.date() < first_day:\n180\t        head = pd.date_range(\n181\t            pd.Timestamp(start.date(), tz=\"UTC\"), frame.index[0], freq=\"1min\", inclusive=\"left\", name=\"timestamp\"\n182\t        )\n183\t        frame = pd.concat([pd.DataFrame(np.nan, index=head, columns=OHLCV_COLUMNS), frame])\n184\t    return frame.loc[start:end]\n185\t\n186\t\n187\tdef prompt_grid(\n188\t    window_start: pd.Timestamp,\n189\t    window_end: pd.Timestamp,\n190\t    cadence_minutes: int,\n191\t    prompt_times: list[pd.Timestamp] | None = None,\n192\t) -> list[pd.Timestamp]:\n193\t    \"\"\"Prompts in [start, end). Filtered with `t < window_end` rather than [:-1] so a window_end\n194\t    not aligned to the cadence does not drop the last valid prompt.\n195\t\n196\t    `prompt_times` replaces the even grid with an explicit list — the start_times the validator\n197\t    actually prompted at, which sit at arbitrary minutes.\"\"\"\n198\t    grid = (\n199\t        prompt_times\n200\t        if prompt_times is not None\n201\t        else pd.date_range(window_start, window_end, freq=f\"{cadence_minutes}min\", tz=\"UTC\")\n202\t    )\n203\t    return [t for t in grid if window_start <= t < window_end]\n204\t\n205\t\n206\tdef generate_day(\n207\t    simulate_fn: Callable,\n208\t    asset: str,\n209\t    day: str,\n210\t    times: list[pd.Timestamp],\n211\t    price_frame: pd.DataFrame,\n212\t    out_dir: Path,\n213\t    time_increment: int,\n214\t    time_length: int,\n215\t    num_simulations: int,\n216\t    issuance_lead: int | None = None,\n217\t    context_mode: str = \"ohlcv\",\n218\t    context_days: int = DEFAULT_CONTEXT_DAYS,\n219\t) -> int:\n220\t    \"\"\"Generate one day's prompts and write the pair. Returns how many were generated, 0 if the\n221\t    day was already covered.\n222\t\n223\t    A day is written whole: if anything is missing it is all regenerated, so a file always holds\n224\t    exactly the start_times its index names and an interrupted run cannot leave a half-day behind.\n225\t    \"\"\"\n226\t    paths_file, index_file = day_files(out_dir, asset, time_length, time_increment, day)\n227\t    wanted = [t.isoformat() for t in times]\n228\t    if not set(wanted) - covered_start_times(index_file, paths_file):\n229\t        return 0\n230\t\n231\t    runs = []\n232\t    head = 0\n233\t    for t in times:\n234\t        # THE no-lookahead line: the context stops at the last bar the prompt's issuance allows,\n235\t        # never at t — the bar labelled t closes after the prompt starts.\n236\t        context = context_slice(price_frame, t, time_length, context_days, issuance_lead)\n237\t        head = max(head, nan_head_minutes(context))\n238\t        if context_mode == \"close\":\n239\t            context = context[\"close\"]\n240\t        out = simulate_fn(\n241\t            asset=asset,\n242\t            start_time=t.isoformat(),\n243\t            time_increment=time_increment,\n244\t            time_length=time_length,\n245\t            num_simulations=num_simulations,\n246\t            context_prices=context,\n247\t        )\n248\t        runs.append(np.asarray(out[2:], dtype=PATH_DTYPE))\n249\t\n250\t    paths_file.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n251\t    stacked = np.stack(runs)\n252\t    np.save(paths_file, stacked)\n253\t    index_file.write_text(\n254\t        json.dumps(\n255\t            {\n256\t                \"start_times\": wanted,\n257\t                \"asset\": asset,\n258\t                \"time_increment\": time_increment,\n259\t                \"time_length\": time_length,\n260\t                \"num_simulations\": int(stacked.shape[1]),"}
