{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Read_62_9e26ea90","content":"1\t\"\"\"Probabilistic price paths calibrated from the supplied minute context.\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\t\n5\timport os\n6\timport random\n7\t\n8\timport numpy as np\n9\t\n10\tCONTEXT_DAYS = 7\n11\tVOL_HALFLIFE_MINUTES = 30.0\n12\t\n13\t\n14\tdef _minute_variance(closes: np.ndarray) -> float:\n15\t    valid_prices = closes[np.isfinite(closes) & (closes > 0)]\n16\t    if valid_prices.size < 11:\n17\t        return 5e-4**2\n18\t    clean = closes.copy()\n19\t    clean[~np.isfinite(clean) | (clean <= 0)] = np.nan\n20\t    rets = np.diff(np.log(clean))\n21\t    rets = rets[np.isfinite(rets)]\n22\t    if rets.size < 10:\n23\t        return 5e-4**2\n24\t    alpha = 1.0 - np.exp(np.log(0.5) / VOL_HALFLIFE_MINUTES)\n25\t    initial = rets[: min(rets.size, 1440)]\n26\t    level = float(np.mean(initial * initial))\n27\t    for ret in rets:\n28\t        level += alpha * (ret * ret - level)\n29\t    return max(level, 1e-12)\n30\t\n31\t\n32\tdef simulate(\n33\t    asset: str,\n34\t    start_time,\n35\t    time_increment: int = 300,\n36\t    time_length: int = 86_400,\n37\t    num_simulations: int = 1000,\n38\t    context_prices=None,\n39\t):\n40\t    seed = int(os.environ.get(\"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\", \"20261108\"))\n41\t    random.seed(seed)\n42\t    np.random.seed(seed)\n43\t    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n44\t\n45\t    closes = context_prices[\"close\"].to_numpy(dtype=float)\n46\t    valid = closes[np.isfinite(closes) & (closes > 0)]\n47\t    last = float(valid[-1]) if valid.size else 1.0\n48\t    minute_variance = _minute_variance(closes)\n49\t    step_sigma = np.sqrt(minute_variance * time_increment / 60.0)\n50\t    steps = time_length // time_increment\n51\t    shocks = rng.normal(0.0, step_sigma, size=(num_simulations, steps))\n52\t    log_paths = np.concatenate(\n53\t        [np.zeros((num_simulations, 1)), np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1)], axis=1\n54\t    )\n55\t    paths = last * np.exp(log_paths)\n56\t    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])"}
{"role":"assistant","content":"The 30-minute EWMA cut BTC-1h CRPS from 519.622 to 453.097 (−12.8%), but worsened BTC-24h and XAU-24h. I’m keeping it only for 1h and testing local-time seasonality on top of the long-window variance estimator for 24h.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"Edit_63_1640a4cc","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/journal.md\",\"old_string\":\"**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\",\"new_string\":\"**Result.** On the latest window, mean CRPS was 3630.894 for BTC-24h (+5.81% versus starter), 2124.964 for XAU-24h (+3.26%), and 453.097 for BTC-1h (−12.80%). On the disjoint older windows, BTC-24h scored 2345.589 on 2026-08-29 to 2026-09-01, XAU-24h 1413.020 on the same dates, and BTC-1h 598.976 on 2026-09-29 to 2026-10-01 with the latest formula. The older BTC-1h no-event gap to best was +6.21%; the latest was +7.61%, down from +50.41% with the starter.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Keep the 30-minute EWMA for 1h; discard it for 24h. The 24h candidate failed the latest-window kill threshold on both test assets. The next 24h experiment starts from the full-context estimator instead.\\n\\n**Lesson.** A forward-variance proxy can favor a fast estimator without implying better multi-horizon CRPS. The 1h volatility term also benefits from a different scale dynamic than 24h price CRPS, so horizon-specific calibration is warranted.\\n\\n## Iteration 2 — New York-time seasonality for 24h\\n\\n**Hypothesis.** For 24h forecasts, a long-window variance estimate multiplied by a causal New York-time-of-day and weekday/weekend profile will beat both the starter and the fast EWMA, especially on XAU and tokenised equities.\\n\\n**Change.** Restore full-context variance for 24h. Estimate mean-absolute-return profiles in 30-minute New York-time bins separately for weekdays and weekends, shrink each type's variance toward the global variance, clip and RMS-normalize the profile, and apply it to future Gaussian increments. Keep the accepted 30-minute EWMA for 1h unchanged. Test BTC, XAU, and TSLAX on latest and September windows.\\n\\n**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Write_64_40a572c4","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/modeling.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Probabilistic price paths calibrated from the supplied minute context.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport os\\nimport random\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport pandas as pd\\n\\nCONTEXT_DAYS = 7\\nVOL_HALFLIFE_MINUTES = 30.0\\n\\n\\ndef _returns(context_prices) -> pd.Series:\\n    closes = context_prices[\\\"close\\\"].astype(float)\\n    closes = closes.where(np.isfinite(closes) & (closes > 0))\\n    return np.log(closes).diff()\\n\\n\\ndef _fast_variance(rets: np.ndarray) -> float:\\n    if rets.size < 10:\\n        return 5e-4**2\\n    alpha = 1.0 - np.exp(np.log(0.5) / VOL_HALFLIFE_MINUTES)\\n    initial = rets[: min(rets.size, 1440)]\\n    level = float(np.mean(initial * initial))\\n    for ret in rets:\\n        level += alpha * (ret * ret - level)\\n    return max(level, 1e-12)\\n\\n\\ndef _seasonal_sigmas(rets: pd.Series, start_time, time_increment: int, steps: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n    values = rets.to_numpy(dtype=float)\\n    valid = np.isfinite(values)\\n    values = values[valid]\\n    if values.size < 100:\\n        return np.full(steps, 5e-4 * np.sqrt(time_increment / 60.0))\\n    local = rets.index[valid].tz_convert(\\\"America/New_York\\\")\\n    weekend = local.day_of_week >= 5\\n    bins = (local.hour * 60 + local.minute) // 30\\n    future = pd.to_datetime(start_time) + pd.to_timedelta(\\n        (np.arange(steps) + 0.5) * time_increment, unit=\\\"s\\\"\\n    )\\n    future_local = future.tz_convert(\\\"America/New_York\\\")\\n    future_weekend = future_local.day_of_week >= 5\\n    future_bins = (future_local.hour * 60 + future_local.minute) // 30\\n    global_variance = max(float(np.var(values)), 1e-12)\\n    sigmas = np.empty(steps)\\n    for is_weekend in (False, True):\\n        future_mask = future_weekend == is_weekend\\n        if not future_mask.any():\\n            continue\\n        history_mask = weekend == is_weekend\\n        count = int(history_mask.sum())\\n        if count < 300:\\n            history_mask = np.ones(values.size, dtype=bool)\\n            count = values.size\\n        sample = values[history_mask]\\n        sample_bins = bins[history_mask]\\n        variance = float(np.mean(sample * sample))\\n        variance = (count * variance + 720 * global_variance) / (count + 720)\\n        mean_absolute = max(float(np.mean(np.abs(sample))), 1e-8)\\n        profile = np.ones(48)\\n        for bucket in range(48):\\n            bucket_values = np.abs(sample[sample_bins == bucket])\\n            if bucket_values.size >= 20:\\n                profile[bucket] = max(float(np.mean(bucket_values)) / mean_absolute, 0.25)\\n        profile = np.clip(profile, 0.25, 3.0)\\n        profile /= np.sqrt(np.mean(profile * profile))\\n        sigmas[future_mask] = np.sqrt(variance * time_increment / 60.0) * profile[\\n            future_bins[future_mask]\\n        ]\\n    return sigmas\\n\\n\\ndef simulate(\\n    asset: str,\\n    start_time,\\n    time_increment: int = 300,\\n    time_length: int = 86_400,\\n    num_simulations: int = 1000,\\n    context_prices=None,\\n):\\n    seed = int(os.environ.get(\\\"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\\\", \\\"20261108\\\"))\\n    random.seed(seed)\\n    np.random.seed(seed)\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\\n\\n    closes = context_prices[\\\"close\\\"].to_numpy(dtype=float)\\n    valid = closes[np.isfinite(closes) & (closes > 0)]\\n    last = float(valid[-1]) if valid.size else 1.0\\n    steps = time_length // time_increment\\n    rets = _returns(context_prices)\\n    if time_length == 3600:\\n        sigma = np.sqrt(_fast_variance(rets.dropna().to_numpy()) * time_increment / 60.0)\\n        sigmas = np.full(steps, sigma)\\n    else:\\n        sigmas = _seasonal_sigmas(rets, start_time, time_increment, steps)\\n    shocks = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, steps)) * sigmas\\n    log_paths = np.concatenate(\\n        [np.zeros((num_simulations, 1)), np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1)], axis=1\\n    )\\n    paths = last * np.exp(log_paths)\\n    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])\\n\"}"}}]}
