{"role":"assistant","content":"Seasonality improved all three latest-window 24h tests by 3.4–5.5%, with the 1h result unchanged. The older-window evidence is mixed, so I’m adding reproducible model-path selection for paired starter comparisons and testing empirical residuals next rather than assuming the gain generalizes.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"Edit_82_dacf5da6","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/predict.py\",\"old_string\":\"from synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import (\\n    context_days_of,\\n    context_slice,\\n    load_minute_prices,\\n    nan_head_minutes,\\n)\\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_ENV, concerns\\n\\n# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\\n# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\\n# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\\nAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\\n\\nimport modeling  # noqa: E402  (import after adding AGENT_DIR to sys.path)\\n\",\"new_string\":\"from synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import (\\n    context_days_of,\\n    context_slice,\\n    load_minute_prices,\\n    load_module,\\n    nan_head_minutes,\\n)\\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import STORE_SUBDIR\\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.event_calendar.events import CALENDAR_ENV, concerns\\n\\n# All paths are resolved from the location of THIS file, never from the cwd: the\\n# script therefore works whether launched from the workspace root (`uv run agent/predict.py`)\\n# or from agent/. The price snapshot is mounted at the workspace root, not inside agent/.\\nAGENT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\\nWORKSPACE = AGENT_DIR.parent\\nsys.path.insert(0, str(AGENT_DIR))\\n\\nmodeling = load_module(Path(os.environ.get(\\\"SYNTH_MODELING_PATH\\\", AGENT_DIR / \\\"modeling.py\\\")))\\n\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Write_83_b38dcb91","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/starter_model.py\",\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Seeded reference copy of the harness starter for paired experiments.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport os\\n\\nimport numpy as np\\n\\nCONTEXT_DAYS = 7\\n\\n\\ndef simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment=300, time_length=86_400, num_simulations=1000, context_prices=None):\\n    steps = time_length // time_increment + 1\\n    closes = context_prices[\\\"close\\\"].dropna()\\n    last = float(closes.iloc[-1])\\n    rets = np.diff(np.log(np.asarray(closes, dtype=float)))\\n    rets = rets[np.isfinite(rets)]\\n    per_step_sigma = float(np.std(rets)) * (time_increment / 60.0) ** 0.5 if rets.size > 10 else 1e-3\\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(int(os.environ.get(\\\"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\\\", \\\"20261108\\\")))\\n    shocks = rng.normal(0.0, per_step_sigma, size=(num_simulations, steps))\\n    shocks[:, 0] = 0.0\\n    paths = last * np.exp(np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1))\\n    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])\\n\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Edit_84_226df205","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/journal.md\",\"old_string\":\"**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\",\"new_string\":\"**Result.** Latest-window mean CRPS: BTC 3315.298 (−3.38% versus starter), XAU 1988.006 (−3.40%), TSLAX 5641.566 (−5.46%). The corresponding no-event gaps to best fell to +6.05%, +15.41%, and +10.79%. September mean CRPS: BTC 2465.831, XAU 1237.493, TSLAX 1674.121. Relative to the fast-EWMA September run, BTC was 5.13% worse and XAU 12.42% better. The 1h regression check reproduced 453.096550 exactly.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Keep seasonality provisionally for 24h, pending paired starter checks on older windows and broader asset coverage. Do not apply it to 1h yet.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Local-time profiles can materially improve short-horizon calibration without changing the 1h code path. A latest-window gain is insufficient: BTC's September result shows that the variance level and seasonal decomposition interact by regime.\\n\\n## Iteration 3 — Empirical 24h residuals\\n\\n**Hypothesis.** Gaussian increments are too concentrated in the tails and insufficiently concentrated near zero. Snapshot 5-minute standardized returns have median absolute values of 0.25–0.46 versus 0.674 for a normal distribution, 99th-percentile absolute values of 3.24–4.10 versus 2.576, and material zero-change mass. Empirical residuals should therefore lower CRPS.\\n\\n**Change.** Keep the Iteration 2 seasonal sigma path, but replace Gaussian 24h shocks with median-centered, winsorized overlapping 5-minute log-return residuals from the supplied context, scaled to unit variance. Keep the 1h Gaussian EWMA path unchanged. Use the same latest and September asset-window cells.\\n\\n**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\"}"}}]}
