{"role":"assistant","content":"The broader 24h result supports keeping the mixture: it improves all 13 September cells and 7 of 13 latest cells, with the latest regressions much smaller than the older gains. I’m now testing only the pre-split calendar effects, with multipliers fitted from early events and late events reserved for validation.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"Grep_177_ca2ada9a","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"summary \\\\(CONTEXT_DAYS\",\"path\":\"/root/.kimi-code/sessions/wd_workspace_c52ddf65534b/session_4d3c2fbb-96c8-43d6-9582-c735ee4b4379/agents/main/tasks/bash-yce4ttx1/output.log\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"head_limit\":10}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Grep_178_a98d2740","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"summary \\\\(CONTEXT_DAYS\",\"path\":\"/root/.kimi-code/sessions/wd_workspace_c52ddf65534b/session_4d3c2fbb-96c8-43d6-9582-c735ee4b4379/agents/main/tasks/bash-hfgtsvx1/output.log\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"head_limit\":10}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Grep_179_70855324","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"summary \\\\(CONTEXT_DAYS\",\"path\":\"/root/.kimi-code/sessions/wd_workspace_c52ddf65534b/session_4d3c2fbb-96c8-43d6-9582-c735ee4b4379/agents/main/tasks/bash-nkyhw2mr/output.log\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"head_limit\":10}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Grep_180_54c7a81b","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"summary \\\\(CONTEXT_DAYS\",\"path\":\"/root/.kimi-code/sessions/wd_workspace_c52ddf65534b/session_4d3c2fbb-96c8-43d6-9582-c735ee4b4379/agents/main/tasks/bash-d2jcvp6w/output.log\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"head_limit\":10}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Write_181_196aa022","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/journal.md\",\"mode\":\"append\",\"content\":\"\\n### Broad 24h validation for Iteration 4\\n\\nAcross all 13 assets, the 50% mixture improved every September cell versus seasonal Gaussian. Relative gains ranged from 1.66% (HYPE) to 8.35% (NVDAX). It also improved 7 of 13 latest cells: all five crypto assets, AAPLX, and WTIOIL. Latest crypto gains were 0.36–0.73%; AAPLX gained 2.62%. The six latest commodity/equity regressions were 0.06–0.70%, except that they must still be monitored. This 20-of-26 cell record, with larger older-window gains than latest-window losses, keeps the mixture as the 24h champion candidate without per-asset selection.\\n\\n## Iteration 7 — Early-fit event multipliers for 24h\\n\\n**Hypothesis.** Scheduled CPI, NFP, FOMC, and earnings releases cause localized volatility that a generic intraday profile cannot fully capture. Conservative multipliers fitted on events before 2026-08-01 should improve later out-of-sample prompts without changing no-event behavior.\\n\\n**Change.** Read only `$SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR` inside `simulate()` and apply multipliers to 24h steps containing or following an in-scope event. Early-fit choices are CPI [3.0, 1.7, 1.3] at 0/5/10 minutes; NFP [1.8, 2.0, 1.1]; FOMC [2.0, 2.5, 1.75], then 1.4 through 60 minutes; earnings [3, 4, 4], 5 through 30 minutes, then 3 through 60 minutes. Exclude PPI, retail sales, GDP/PCE, and EIA because their early/late evidence was weak, unstable, or collinear. Cap the combined multiplier at 8. Validate on the late NFP window, September CPI/FOMC, October CPI/FOMC and earnings, and require no-event predictions to remain exactly unchanged. The 1h path is unchanged in this iteration.\\n\\n**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Edit_182_25aa50aa","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/modeling.py\",\"old_string\":\"def simulate(\\n    asset: str,\\n\",\"new_string\":\"def _event_multipliers(asset: str, start_time, time_increment: int, steps: int) -> np.ndarray:\\n    multipliers = np.ones(steps)\\n    path = os.environ.get(\\\"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR\\\")\\n    if not path:\\n        return multipliers\\n    try:\\n        events = pd.read_parquet(path, columns=[\\\"time_utc\\\", \\\"event\\\", \\\"scope\\\"])\\n        events[\\\"time_utc\\\"] = pd.to_datetime(events[\\\"time_utc\\\"], utc=True)\\n        start = pd.Timestamp(start_time)\\n        if start.tzinfo is None:\\n            start = start.tz_localize(\\\"UTC\\\")\\n        else:\\n            start = start.tz_convert(\\\"UTC\\\")\\n        scope = events[\\\"scope\\\"].astype(str)\\n        relevant = events[\\\"event\\\"].isin([\\\"CPI\\\", \\\"NFP\\\", \\\"FOMC\\\", \\\"EARNINGS\\\"])\\n        relevant &= (scope == \\\"all\\\") | scope.str.split(\\\",\\\").apply(lambda values: asset in values)\\n        finish = start + pd.Timedelta(seconds=steps * time_increment)\\n        events = events[relevant & (events[\\\"time_utc\\\"] >= start) & (events[\\\"time_utc\\\"] <= finish)]\\n        ends = start + pd.to_timedelta(np.arange(1, steps + 1) * time_increment, unit=\\\"s\\\")\\n        starts = ends - pd.Timedelta(seconds=time_increment)\\n        profiles = {\\n            \\\"CPI\\\": [3.0, 1.7, 1.3],\\n            \\\"NFP\\\": [1.8, 2.0, 1.1],\\n            \\\"FOMC\\\": [2.0, 2.5, 1.75] + [1.4] * 10,\\n            \\\"EARNINGS\\\": [3.0, 4.0, 4.0] + [5.0] * 4 + [3.0] * 6,\\n        }\\n        for event in events.itertuples():\\n            containing = np.flatnonzero((starts < event.time_utc) & (ends >= event.time_utc))\\n            first = int(containing[0]) if containing.size else 0\\n            for offset, value in enumerate(profiles[event.event]):\\n                index = first + offset\\n                if index >= steps:\\n                    break\\n                multipliers[index] *= value\\n    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError, AttributeError):\\n        return np.ones(steps)\\n    return np.clip(multipliers, 1.0, 8.0)\\n\\n\\ndef simulate(\\n    asset: str,\\n\"}"}}]}
