{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"Grep_225_5f501ca8","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"summary \\\\(CONTEXT_DAYS\",\"path\":\"/root/.kimi-code/sessions/wd_workspace_c52ddf65534b/session_4d3c2fbb-96c8-43d6-9582-c735ee4b4379/agents/main/tasks/bash-6dhojs3n/output.log\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"head_limit\":5}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Grep_226_c5947bed","function":{"name":"Grep","arguments":"{\"pattern\":\"summary \\\\(CONTEXT_DAYS\",\"path\":\"/root/.kimi-code/sessions/wd_workspace_c52ddf65534b/session_4d3c2fbb-96c8-43d6-9582-c735ee4b4379/agents/main/tasks/bash-5wyjamsg/output.log\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"head_limit\":5}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Write_227_38d757b3","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/journal.md\",\"mode\":\"append\",\"content\":\"\\n## Iteration 9 — Sixty-minute block bootstrap for 1h\\n\\n**Hypothesis.** Independent empirical increments preserve the marginal residual distribution but destroy volatility clustering and runs of zero changes. Sampling contiguous 60-minute residual paths should improve the 5-, 15-, and 60-minute realized-volatility CRPS without changing the intended marginal calibration.\\n\\n**Change.** Add a research-only switch that samples each simulated path from one contiguous 60-minute context residual block, rather than drawing 60 independent residuals. Keep the 30-minute EWMA scale and all 24h behavior fixed. Compare against the independent-empirical results on all five crypto assets in latest and October windows.\\n\\n**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Edit_228_7972c6e9","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/modeling.py\",\"old_string\":\"            residual = np.clip(residual - np.median(residual), -8.0, 8.0)\\n            shocks = residual[rng.integers(0, residual.size, size=(num_simulations, steps))] * sigmas\\n        else:\\n            shocks = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, steps)) * sigmas\\n\",\"new_string\":\"            residual = np.clip(residual - np.median(residual), -8.0, 8.0)\\n            block_minutes = int(os.environ.get(\\\"SYNTH_1H_BLOCK_MINUTES\\\", \\\"1\\\"))\\n            if block_minutes == steps and residual.size > steps:\\n                starts = rng.integers(0, residual.size - steps + 1, size=num_simulations)\\n                indices = starts[:, None] + np.arange(steps)[None, :]\\n                shocks = residual[indices] * sigmas\\n            else:\\n                shocks = residual[rng.integers(0, residual.size, size=(num_simulations, steps))] * sigmas\\n        else:\\n            shocks = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, steps)) * sigmas\\n\"}"}}]}
