{"role":"assistant","content":"The 60-minute bootstrap is not robust: October’s mean CRPS slightly worsens, led by ETH, so I’m rejecting the long block rather than optimizing on the latest window. Antithetic sampling improves five of six 24h cells and stays provisionally accepted. I’ll test shorter blocks and 1h seasonality independently.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"Read_245_66d2ff3d","function":{"name":"Read","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/modeling.py\",\"line_offset\":128,\"n_lines\":55}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Edit_246_d9d531ff","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/journal.md\",\"old_string\":\"**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\\n## Iteration 10 — Antithetic ensemble sampling\\n\",\"new_string\":\"**Result.** Latest 60-minute block CRPS, versus independent empirical: BTC 443.297 (−1.08%), ETH 562.116 (−1.48%), SOL 728.232 (−0.64%), XRP 935.250 (+0.22%), HYPE 915.849 (−0.23%). October: BTC 598.657 (+0.25%), ETH 735.618 (+0.52%), SOL 1056.507 (+0.20%), XRP 1193.429 (−0.21%), HYPE 1284.966 (−0.04%). The October mean relative change across assets was approximately +0.14%, so the long block failed the two-window rule despite four latest gains.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Discard the 60-minute block. Test 15-minute concatenated blocks as a bounded follow-up: preserving short-run clustering may help without carrying a stale hour-long regime.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Marginal residual matching does not guarantee good path-level calibration, but a structure that only helps the latest regime is not acceptable. Long blocks can preserve outdated volatility and trend as well as useful clustering.\\n\\n## Iteration 10 — Antithetic ensemble sampling\\n\"}"}}]}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"Read_245_66d2ff3d","content":"128\t    closes = context_prices[\"close\"].to_numpy(dtype=float)\n129\t    valid = closes[np.isfinite(closes) & (closes > 0)]\n130\t    last = float(valid[-1]) if valid.size else 1.0\n131\t    steps = time_length // time_increment\n132\t    rets = _returns(context_prices)\n133\t    if time_length == 3600:\n134\t        minute_values = rets.dropna().to_numpy()\n135\t        sigma = np.sqrt(_fast_variance(minute_values) * time_increment / 60.0)\n136\t        sigmas = np.full(steps, sigma)\n137\t        if minute_values.size >= 100:\n138\t            residual = minute_values / max(float(np.std(minute_values)), 1e-8)\n139\t            residual = np.clip(residual - np.median(residual), -8.0, 8.0)\n140\t            block_minutes = int(os.environ.get(\"SYNTH_1H_BLOCK_MINUTES\", \"1\"))\n141\t            if block_minutes == steps and residual.size > steps:\n142\t                starts = rng.integers(0, residual.size - steps + 1, size=num_simulations)\n143\t                indices = starts[:, None] + np.arange(steps)[None, :]\n144\t                shocks = residual[indices] * sigmas\n145\t            else:\n146\t                shocks = residual[rng.integers(0, residual.size, size=(num_simulations, steps))] * sigmas\n147\t        else:\n148\t            shocks = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, steps)) * sigmas\n149\t    else:\n150\t        sigmas = _seasonal_sigmas(rets, start_time, time_increment, steps)\n151\t        sigmas *= _event_multipliers(asset, start_time, time_increment, steps)\n152\t        clean = context_prices[\"close\"].astype(float)\n153\t        clean = clean.where(np.isfinite(clean) & (clean > 0))\n154\t        five_minute = np.log(clean).diff(5).dropna().to_numpy()\n155\t        minute_values = rets.dropna().to_numpy()\n156\t        if five_minute.size >= 100 and minute_values.size >= 100:\n157\t            residual = five_minute / np.sqrt(5.0 * max(float(np.var(minute_values)), 1e-12))\n158\t            residual = np.clip(residual - np.median(residual), -8.0, 8.0)\n159\t            empirical = residual[rng.integers(0, residual.size, size=(num_simulations, steps))] * sigmas\n160\t            gaussian = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, steps)) * sigmas\n161\t            shocks = np.where(rng.random((num_simulations, steps)) < 0.5, empirical, gaussian)\n162\t        else:\n163\t            shocks = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, steps)) * sigmas\n164\t    if os.environ.get(\"SYNTH_ANTITHETIC\") == \"1\":\n165\t        half = num_simulations // 2\n166\t        shocks[half : 2 * half] = -shocks[:half]\n167\t    log_paths = np.concatenate(\n168\t        [np.zeros((num_simulations, 1)), np.cumsum(shocks, axis=1)], axis=1\n169\t    )\n170\t    paths = last * np.exp(log_paths)\n171\t    return (start_time, time_increment, *[p.tolist() for p in paths])"}
