{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"Edit_248_37054379","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/journal.md\",\"old_string\":\"**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\",\"new_string\":\"**Result.** Antithetic versus ordinary sampling on latest: BTC 3295.243 versus 3301.220 (−0.18%), XAU 1983.055 versus 1989.245 (−0.31%), TSLAX 5668.740 versus 5674.022 (−0.09%). September: BTC 2412.655 versus 2416.956 (−0.18%), XAU 1211.321 versus 1210.388 (+0.08%), TSLAX 1608.422 versus 1614.949 (−0.40%). Five of six cells improved; all effects were small.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Keep antithetic sampling under the signed-consistency rule, then verify it on the final all-asset model. It is not a substitute for calibration.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Removing finite-ensemble mean error gives a small, low-risk gain without changing the target distribution or path count.\\n\\n## Iteration 11 — Short blocks and 1h local-time seasonality\\n\\n**Hypothesis.** Two independent additions may address remaining 1h errors: 15-minute concatenated residual blocks can preserve short-run volatility clustering without the 60-minute block's stale regime; a New York-time profile normalized to unit daily RMS can capture predictable intraday volatility without changing the current EWMA level.\\n\\n**Change.** Test the two arms independently against independent-empirical 1h results on all five crypto assets in latest and October windows. Arm A concatenates randomly selected 15-minute residual blocks. Arm B uses independent residuals with a seasonal sigma profile. Do not combine them unless each succeeds; do not change the 24h model.\\n\\n**Result.** Pending.\\n\\n**Verdict.** Pending.\\n\\n**Lesson.** Pending.\\n\"}"}},{"type":"function","id":"Edit_249_4a5cbe38","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"agent/modeling.py\",\"old_string\":\"    if time_length == 3600:\\n        minute_values = rets.dropna().to_numpy()\\n        sigma = np.sqrt(_fast_variance(minute_values) * time_increment / 60.0)\\n        sigmas = np.full(steps, sigma)\\n        if minute_values.size >= 100:\\n            residual = minute_values / max(float(np.std(minute_values)), 1e-8)\\n            residual = np.clip(residual - np.median(residual), -8.0, 8.0)\\n            block_minutes = int(os.environ.get(\\\"SYNTH_1H_BLOCK_MINUTES\\\", \\\"1\\\"))\\n            if block_minutes == steps and residual.size > steps:\\n                starts = rng.integers(0, residual.size - steps + 1, size=num_simulations)\\n                indices = starts[:, None] + np.arange(steps)[None, :]\\n                shocks = residual[indices] * sigmas\\n            else:\\n                shocks = residual[rng.integers(0, residual.size, size=(num_simulations, steps))] * sigmas\\n        else:\\n            shocks = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, steps)) * sigmas\\n\",\"new_string\":\"    if time_length == 3600:\\n        minute_values = rets.dropna().to_numpy()\\n        sigma = np.sqrt(_fast_variance(minute_values) * time_increment / 60.0)\\n        sigmas = np.full(steps, sigma)\\n        if os.environ.get(\\\"SYNTH_1H_SEASONAL\\\") == \\\"1\\\":\\n            profile = _seasonal_sigmas(rets, start_time, time_increment, 1440)\\n            profile /= np.sqrt(np.mean(profile * profile))\\n            sigmas = np.full(steps, sigma) * profile[:steps]\\n        if minute_values.size >= 100:\\n            residual = minute_values / max(float(np.std(minute_values)), 1e-8)\\n            residual = np.clip(residual - np.median(residual), -8.0, 8.0)\\n            block_minutes = int(os.environ.get(\\\"SYNTH_1H_BLOCK_MINUTES\\\", \\\"1\\\"))\\n            if block_minutes > 1 and residual.size > block_minutes:\\n                n_blocks = (steps + block_minutes - 1) // block_minutes\\n                starts = rng.integers(\\n                    0, residual.size - block_minutes + 1, size=(num_simulations, n_blocks)\\n                )\\n                indices = (starts[:, :, None] + np.arange(block_minutes)[None, None, :]).reshape(\\n                    num_simulations, n_blocks * block_minutes\\n                )[:, :steps]\\n                shocks = residual[indices] * sigmas\\n            else:\\n                shocks = residual[rng.integers(0, residual.size, size=(num_simulations, steps))] * sigmas\\n        else:\\n            shocks = rng.normal(size=(num_simulations, steps)) * sigmas\\n\"}"}}]}
